  "id": "electrocochleography",
  "term": "electrocochleography",
  "definition": "Electrocochleography is an electrophysiological method used during cochlear implant surgery to monitor cochlear responses while the electrode is being inserted. It is used to give immediate feedback that may help reduce injury to the inner ear and support preservation of any remaining natural hearing.",
